# Global .ignore — read by ripgrep, fd, and fff during directory traversal.
# Symlinked to ~/.ignore, so it applies to anything searched under $HOME.
#
# The ignore crate ranks .ignore above .gitignore, so a negation here
# re-includes a file that .gitignore excludes WITHOUT disabling the rest of
# .gitignore (node_modules, vendor, … stay filtered). This is what lets fff's
# <leader>p surface gitignored files like .env.

# Env files — gitignored in projects, but I want them one keystroke away.
!.env
!.env.*
